# Phase C prompt-assembly verification against real project data — contains
# real sensitive content by construction (the "before" capture has to, to
# prove the "after" one excludes it). Never commit these; regenerate locally
# per supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-c-verification/README.md.
# The synthetic fixture pair in the same directory is fabricated data and is
# committed deliberately — this rule does not apply to it.
supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-c-verification/before.json
supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-c-verification/after.json
supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-c-verification/prompt-before.txt
supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-c-verification/prompt-after.txt

# Phase E1 feed-forward verification — same reasoning as Phase C above, and
# this one additionally captures a real approved direction_versions row
# (previousApproved.content), which is exactly the leak path being proven
# closed. Never commit these; regenerate locally per
# supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-e1-verification/README.md.
supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-e1-verification/before.json
supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-e1-verification/after.json
supabase/functions/approve-direction/phase-e1-verification/prompt-before.txt
